        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") ...) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U5 | SKYLAB SKW92A ... | Main compute / WiFi radio / 5-port Ethernet switch"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Grounding both sides of the LAN3 transmit pair can clamp or short the module's Ethernet PHY signals, making that port unusable and potentially stressing the PHY.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist directly connects both SKW92A LAN_PORT3 transmit pins to GND. This is inconsistent with normal Ethernet differential-pair practice and can impair or stress the module's PHY."
}

